IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part IV: the two pilot projects that calculate the rate of weekly benefits on the claimant's 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings:
-- Pilot Project No. 11 (reg 77.7) and Pilot Project No. 16 (reg 77.93). Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt.
-- The text is an unofficial rendering; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- The two regs say the same thing in the same words in paragraphs (3)(a) to (f) and (4); they differ in their windows, their Schedule, and who they exclude.
-- So each rule stated twice in the text is stated once here and cites both (the keel's way with ss 6(2) and 152.01(5)); what differs is a rule apiece.
-- Both projects are spent (Pilot Project No. 16 closed for benefit periods established after April 6, 2013). The date of establishment is a plain input.
-- Relations (Hohfeld): the project gives each claimant it includes a rate worked out on the 14 highest weeks (a claim; the Commission bears the duty); (4) binds the Commission to allocate pay-period earnings.

§ `Regulations Part IV - Pilot Projects on the rate of weekly benefits`

§§ `Reg 77.7(1) and reg 77.93(1) - purposes`

-- src:1444 | 77.7 (1) Pilot Project No. 11 is established for the purpose of testing whether paying benefits based on calculating the rate of weekly benefits using the insurable earnings from a claimant’s 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in the qualifying period would encourage claimants to accept all available work.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(1) (src:1444)
`reg 77.7(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 11` MEANS
    "testing whether paying benefits based on calculating the rate of weekly benefits using the insurable earnings from a claimant’s 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in the qualifying period would encourage claimants to accept all available work"

-- src:1497 | 77.93 (1) Pilot Project No. 16 is established for the purpose of testing whether paying benefits based on a rate of weekly benefits calculated using the insurable earnings from a claimant’s 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in the qualifying period would encourage claimants to accept all available work.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.93(1) (src:1497)
`reg 77.93(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 16` MEANS
    "testing whether paying benefits based on a rate of weekly benefits calculated using the insurable earnings from a claimant’s 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in the qualifying period would encourage claimants to accept all available work"

§§ `Reg 77.7(2) - who is included in Pilot Project No. 11`

-- src:1445 | (2) Pilot Project No. 11 applies in respect of every claimant whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on October 26, 2008 and ending on June 25, 2011 and who is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.8, other than a claimant in respect of whom the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations apply.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(2) (src:1445)
`reg 77.7(2) the period in which the benefit period must be established for Pilot Project No. 11` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2008 10 26), (YearMonthDay 2011 6 25)

-- Pilot Project No. 11 applies to every claimant whose benefit period is established in the period from October 26, 2008 to June 25, 2011 and who is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I
-- that is set out in Schedule II.8, other than a claimant in respect of whom the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations apply.
-- src:1445 | (2) Pilot Project No. 11 applies in respect of every claimant whose benefit period is established in the period beginning on October 26, 2008 and ending on June 25, 2011 and who is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.8, other than a claimant in respect of whom the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations apply.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(2) (src:1445)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period is established` IS A DATE
      `the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.8` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Schedule II.8 (piece er6)
      `the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations apply in respect of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.7(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11` IF
        `the day` `the day on which the benefit period is established` `falls within` `reg 77.7(2) the period in which the benefit period must be established for Pilot Project No. 11`
    AND `the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.8`
    AND (NOT `the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations apply in respect of the claimant`)

