§§ `Reg 77.7(3)(a) to (d) and reg 77.93(3)(a) to (d) - what the project switches off, and the period it reads instead`

-- (a) subsections 14(2), (4) and (4.1) of the Act do not apply, and (d) section 24.2 of these Regulations does not apply, for a claimant included in the project.
-- src:1447 | (a) subsections 14(2), (4) and (4.1) of the Act do not apply;
-- src:1450 | (d) section 24.2 of these Regulations does not apply;
-- src:1500 | (a) subsections 14(2), (4) and (4.1) of the Act do not apply;
-- src:1503 | (d) section 24.2 does not apply;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(3)(a), reg 77.7(3)(d), reg 77.93(3)(a), reg 77.93(3)(d) (src:1447) (src:1450) (src:1500) (src:1503)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11 or Pilot Project No. 16` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.7(3)(a), (d) and reg 77.93(3)(a), (d) subsections 14(2), (4) and (4.1) of the Act and section 24.2 of the Regulations do not apply` IF
    `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11 or Pilot Project No. 16`

-- (b) the reference in s 14(3) of the Act, and (c) the references in s 24.1 of these Regulations, to "the rate calculation period" are read as references to "the qualifying period" for a claimant included in the project.
-- The period such a reference reads is the qualifying period for an included claimant, and the rate calculation period for anyone else.
-- src:1448 | (b) the reference in subsection 14(3) of the Act to “the rate calculation period” shall be read as a reference to “the qualifying period”;
-- src:1449 | (c) the references in section 24.1 of these Regulations to “the rate calculation period” shall be read as references to “the qualifying period”;
-- src:1501 | (b) the reference in subsection 14(3) of the Act to “the rate calculation period” shall be read as a reference to “the qualifying period”;
-- src:1502 | (c) the references in section 24.1 to “the rate calculation period” shall be read as references to “the qualifying period”;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(3)(b), reg 77.7(3)(c), reg 77.93(3)(b), reg 77.93(3)(c) (src:1448-1449) (src:1501-1502)
GIVEN `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11 or Pilot Project No. 16` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate calculation period` IS A `Period of days` -- out of range: s 14(3) of the Act (piece ei1)
      `the qualifying period` IS A `Period of days` -- out of range: s 8 of the Act (piece ei1)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `reg 77.7(3)(b), (c) and reg 77.93(3)(b), (c) the period that the reference to the rate calculation period reads as` IS
    IF `the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11 or Pilot Project No. 16`
    THEN `the qualifying period`
    ELSE `the rate calculation period`

§§ `Reg 77.7(3)(e), (f) and reg 77.93(3)(e), (f) - the weekly insurable earnings`

-- (e) the insurable earnings in the qualifying period are the aggregate of (i) the insurable earnings from the 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in that period, not including any insurable earnings paid or payable
-- under section 24.1, and (ii) any insurable earnings paid or payable in the qualifying period under section 24.1; (f) the weekly insurable earnings are those earnings divided by 14.
-- Readings taken (fork F-reg77.7e): the 14 highest weeks are picked from the weekly earnings with the section 24.1 earnings taken out; a qualifying period with fewer than 14 weeks of earnings sums the weeks it has and still divides by 14.
-- src:1451 | (e) the insurable earnings in a claimant’s qualifying period shall be the aggregate of
-- src:1452 | (i) the insurable earnings from the 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in that period, not including any insurable earnings paid or payable to the claimant in the qualifying period under section 24.1, and
-- src:1453 | (ii) any insurable earnings paid or payable to the claimant in the qualifying period under section 24.1; and
-- src:1454 | (f) a claimant’s weekly insurable earnings shall be determined by dividing the insurable earnings in the claimant’s qualifying period, determined in accordance with paragraph (e), by 14.
-- src:1504 | (e) the insurable earnings in a claimant’s qualifying period shall be the aggregate of
-- src:1505 | (i) the insurable earnings from the 14 highest weeks of insurable earnings in that period, not including any insurable earnings paid or payable to the claimant in the qualifying period under section 24.1, and
-- src:1506 | (ii) any insurable earnings paid or payable to the claimant in the qualifying period under section 24.1; and
-- src:1507 | (f) a claimant’s weekly insurable earnings shall be determined by dividing the insurable earnings in the claimant’s qualifying period, determined in accordance with paragraph (e), by 14.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(3)(e), reg 77.7(3)(f), reg 77.93(3)(e), reg 77.93(3)(f) (src:1451-1454) (src:1504-1507)
GIVEN `the insurable earnings of each week of the qualifying period, not including any paid or payable under section 24.1` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the insurable earnings paid or payable in the qualifying period under section 24.1` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: reg 24.1 (piece er2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.7(3)(e), (f) and reg 77.93(3)(e), (f) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` IS
    ((sum (take 14 (reverse (sort `the insurable earnings of each week of the qualifying period, not including any paid or payable under section 24.1`))))
        PLUS `the insurable earnings paid or payable in the qualifying period under section 24.1`) DIVIDED BY 14

§§ `Reg 77.7(4) and reg 77.93(4) - earnings reported by pay period`

-- (4) If a claimant's insurable earnings have been reported on the record of employment by pay period, the Commission shall (a) allocate the amount proportionately over the pay period; or
-- (b) if the claimant or the employer provides evidence of the amount actually earned in any week within the pay period, allocate the amount proportionately over the other weeks in that pay period.
-- "Proportionately" is read by days: a week takes the share of the amount that its days in the pay period are of the days of the pay period (fork F-reg77.7f); a pay period of whole weeks shares equally.
-- src:1455 | (4) If a claimant’s insurable earnings have been reported on the record of employment by pay period, the Commission shall
-- src:1456 | (a) allocate the amount of insurable earnings proportionately over the pay period; or
-- src:1457 | (b) if the claimant or the employer provides evidence of the amount of insurable earnings actually earned by the claimant in any week within the pay period, allocate the amount of insurable earnings proportionately over the other weeks in that pay period.
-- src:1508 | (4) If a claimant’s insurable earnings have been reported on the record of employment by pay period, the Commission shall
-- src:1509 | (a) allocate the amount of insurable earnings proportionately over the pay period; or
-- src:1510 | (b) if the claimant or the employer provides evidence of the amount of insurable earnings actually earned by the claimant in any week within the pay period, allocate the amount of insurable earnings proportionately over the other weeks in that pay period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(4), reg 77.93(4) (src:1455-1457) (src:1508-1510)
GIVEN `the insurable earnings reported on the record of employment for the pay period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of the week that fall in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.7(4)(a) and reg 77.93(4)(a) the insurable earnings allocated to the week` IS
    IF `the number of days in the pay period` ABOVE 0
    THEN JUST (`the insurable earnings reported on the record of employment for the pay period` TIMES (`the number of days of the week that fall in the pay period` DIVIDED BY `the number of days in the pay period`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1457 | (b) if the claimant or the employer provides evidence of the amount of insurable earnings actually earned by the claimant in any week within the pay period, allocate the amount of insurable earnings proportionately over the other weeks in that pay period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(4)(b), reg 77.93(4)(b) (src:1457)
GIVEN `the insurable earnings reported on the record of employment for the pay period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of the week that fall in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts of insurable earnings actually earned in the weeks for which evidence is provided` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the number of days of those weeks that fall in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.7(4)(b) and reg 77.93(4)(b) the insurable earnings allocated to one of the other weeks` IS
    IF `the number of days in the pay period` ABOVE `the number of days of those weeks that fall in the pay period`
    THEN JUST ((`the insurable earnings reported on the record of employment for the pay period` MINUS (sum `the amounts of insurable earnings actually earned in the weeks for which evidence is provided`))
                TIMES (`the number of days of the week that fall in the pay period` DIVIDED BY (`the number of days in the pay period` MINUS `the number of days of those weeks that fall in the pay period`)))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4) as a whole: the Commission applies (b) when the claimant or the employer provides evidence of the amount actually earned in a week of the pay period, and (a) otherwise.
-- src:1455 | (4) If a claimant’s insurable earnings have been reported on the record of employment by pay period, the Commission shall
-- src:1456 | (a) allocate the amount of insurable earnings proportionately over the pay period; or
-- src:1457 | (b) if the claimant or the employer provides evidence of the amount of insurable earnings actually earned by the claimant in any week within the pay period, allocate the amount of insurable earnings proportionately over the other weeks in that pay period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.7(4), reg 77.93(4) (src:1455-1457)
GIVEN `the insurable earnings reported on the record of employment for the pay period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of the week that fall in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant or the employer provides evidence of the amount of insurable earnings actually earned in a week within the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts of insurable earnings actually earned in the weeks for which evidence is provided` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the number of days of those weeks that fall in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 77.7(4) and reg 77.93(4) the insurable earnings allocated to a week with no evidence of its own` IS
    IF `the claimant or the employer provides evidence of the amount of insurable earnings actually earned in a week within the pay period`
    THEN `reg 77.7(4)(b) and reg 77.93(4)(b) the insurable earnings allocated to one of the other weeks` `the insurable earnings reported on the record of employment for the pay period` `the number of days in the pay period` `the number of days of the week that fall in the pay period` `the amounts of insurable earnings actually earned in the weeks for which evidence is provided` `the number of days of those weeks that fall in the pay period`
    ELSE `reg 77.7(4)(a) and reg 77.93(4)(a) the insurable earnings allocated to the week` `the insurable earnings reported on the record of employment for the pay period` `the number of days in the pay period` `the number of days of the week that fall in the pay period`
